<section class="card" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-heading">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h2 id="walkthrough-heading" class="h4">Integration walkthrough</h2>
    <p>This public path uses only original synthetic fields. It never loads private holdings, account identifiers, credentials, or raw provider payloads.</p>

    <figure aria-labelledby="architecture-caption">
      <figcaption id="architecture-caption" class="fw-bold">Implemented synthetic architecture</figcaption>
      <ol class="demo-flow" data-testid="architecture-diagram">
        <li>Reviewer browser <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>Rails route / controller <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>DemoPortfolio fictional inputs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>PortfolioAnalytics decimal calculations <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>ERB / helper accessible HTML</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">Each arrow is an in-process read or rendered response, not a separate deployable service. No database or provider adapter is in this data path.</p>
    </figure>

    <figure aria-labelledby="request-caption">
      <figcaption id="request-caption" class="fw-bold">Implemented request flow</figcaption>
      <ol class="demo-flow" data-testid="request-flow-diagram">
        <li>GET /portfolio_demo?scenario=complete <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>Validate allowlisted scenario <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>Build fresh fictional inputs or explicit unavailable preview <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>Normalize / calculate if evidence exists <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></li>
        <li>Return HTML with no-store policy</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">Scenario selection is a read-only GET. Unknown or structured scenarios return HTTP 400; there is no demo write or refresh endpoint.</p>
    </figure>

    <details>
      <summary>Inspect the sanitized synthetic shape and normalization</summary>
      <p>This fixed DEMO-A example is independent of the selected scenario. It is an illustrative normalized shape, not a provider response or evidence that a provider supports these fields.</p>
      <pre class="demo-json" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Sanitized fictional example"><code><%= demo_walkthrough_json %></code></pre>
      <p>Identity requires a valid unique ticker and nonblank name. Quantities and costs are nonnegative finite decimals; supplied prices must be positive finite decimals.
        JSON decimal strings preserve precision. Missing price or cost remains null internally, never zero.
        Optional observation and receipt timestamps are validated separately as ISO 8601 with time zones and normalized to UTC.
        Unknown observation time stays unknown even if a receipt time exists. Missing prices have no price provenance.
        The synthetic source and observation time are declared fixture metadata; no provider receipt time or delay is asserted.</p>
      <p>Quantity, unit cost, price, identity, and observation time are fictional inputs. Value, cost basis, gain/loss, and weight follow the published formulas, not an AI model.</p>
    </details>

    <h3 class="h5 mt-3">Cache, freshness, and failures</h3>
    <p>Implemented policy: reconstruct static inputs on each request; no provider cache, polling, refresh jobs, database persistence, or external calls.
      HTML uses <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>. Reloading does not update the fictional observation time or make it live.</p>
    <p>Missing price makes total valuation and aggregate gain/loss unavailable; missing cost makes cost and gain/loss unavailable.
      Empty holdings retain zero sums, not invented positions. Loading and provider-error scenarios are explicitly simulated unavailable previews, not real requests or successful fallback data.</p>

    <h3 class="h5">Provider-backed extension — gated, not implemented here</h3>
    <p>The existing watchlist lookup is not a timestamped holdings contract. A future adapter must first verify endpoint fields, subscription entitlements, display/distribution rights,
      delay, quotas, caching/retention rights, and supported instruments. No TTL or real-time freshness promise is invented.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Authorize an explicit bounded refresh on the server; keep credentials out of the browser and public walkthrough.</li>
      <li>Read permitted provider evidence; validate identity, currency, decimals, source observation time, receipt time, and quality separately.</li>
      <li>Store only permitted snapshots under a verified retention policy, with bounded retries, deduplication, and quota handling.</li>
      <li>Render valid evidence or explicit unavailable / delayed / stale / error states. Authentication, rate-limit, timeout, malformed-response, or entitlement failures must never trigger synthetic success.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mb-0">Any retained permitted snapshot must keep its original observation time and visible refresh failure, never a falsely fresh timestamp.
      Private Kraken reads and any separately approved executor remain outside this public demo.</p>
  </div>
</section>
